@host = http://localhost:7071

### A basic model code that exists in your imported catalogue. Everything below uses it.
@basicModelCode = AXAA54

### A VIN to reach the same menu from the other end. Only used by the vehicle section at the bottom,
### which needs the CompanyData/Vehicles containers this sample does not provision.
@vin = JTMHX01J8L4198293

### ─────────────────────────────── replicate ───────────────────────────────

### Full backfill — re-syncs EVERY menu row into Cosmos, not just the dirty ones.
### Run this to switch replication on for an existing catalogue, after rebuilding a container, or
### after the system-wide parts-price update (which leaves MenuItem rows clean, so only a full pass
### repairs their documents).
###
### The hourly timers are disabled locally; this endpoint is how you replicate while developing.
###
### The response carries the same per-table counts as replication-status below. A sweep that failed
### to write some rows finishes exactly like one that wrote them all, so read `status.pending` rather
### than the status code — and if it is non-zero, just run this again.
POST {{host}}/api/replicate-all

### How far replication has got — per table: total rows, never replicated, still pending.
### `isUpToDate: true` is what a finished backfill looks like.
GET {{host}}/api/replication-status

### ─────────────────────────── sync to DuckDB ───────────────────────────

### Syncs every menu table from SQL into ONE DuckDB database file (menus.duckdb beside the host, or
### ConnectionStrings:DuckDB), one table after another — the local-file counterpart of replicate-all,
### and the store the DuckDB-backed menu lookup reads.
###
### Incremental by default: each table pulls only the rows saved at or past ITS OWN destination-side
### MAX(LastSaveDate) watermark; the first run over a fresh file is automatically a full pull. No
### configuration is needed — DuckDB has no server.
###
### The response reports each table: `succeeded`, `upserted`, `pruned`, and the `watermark` the pull
### started from (null = full pull). Read those rather than the status code — a failed table does not
### stop the run, and rerunning is idempotent. One writer at a time: do not overlap two of these.
POST {{host}}/api/duckdb-sync

### Full reload — every table re-pulls EVERYTHING and prunes rows whose ids left SQL. This is the
### reconciler for hard deletes (an incremental pull cannot see a row that no longer exists), the
### DuckDB counterpart of replicate-all's updateAll. Run it on a schedule, or after a bulk cleanup.
POST {{host}}/api/duckdb-sync?fullReload=true

### ...then read the menu back FROM DUCKDB. Same parameters, same response shape and — the claim
### worth testing — the same answer as GET api/menu/{code} below, because everything above the
### storage seam is identical; only the storage differs. Run duckdb-sync, then call both endpoints
### for one code and diff them.
###
### Answers 503 with a pointer at duckdb-sync when the store was never synced (a missing file is
### never silently created; the lookup opens it read-only).
GET {{host}}/api/menu-duckdb/{{basicModelCode}}

### The language / country / free-filter variants work identically to the Cosmos endpoint.
GET {{host}}/api/menu-duckdb/{{basicModelCode}}?language=ar&countryId=2

### ──────────────────────────── then read it back ────────────────────────────

### The service menu for one basic model code — the read side of everything above.
### One single-partition query, then the SAME generator the DMS export uses, so the codes here are the
### codes the dealer's DMS received. Run this after replicate-all and compare against the export.
###
### Returns the variants of the model, each with:
###   periodicServices  — the scheduled services, ordered by distance
###   standaloneServices — the ones sold on their own
### and per line: code, labourCode, parts with prices, and the discounted totalPrice.
###
### `notFound: true` means nothing is replicated under this model code — run replicate-all first.
### It is NOT the same as a menu that exists but generates no lines (every variant deleted, or
### intervals whose groups carry no labour detail), which returns notFound: false with no services.
###
### There is no dealer cost anywhere in the response, by construction — the lookup never asks the
### generator for it.
GET {{host}}/api/menu/{{basicModelCode}}

### The same menu in another language. Menu codes are language-dependent (the prefixes, postfixes and
### operation codes are multi-language), so correlate lines across languages by `lineKey`, never by
### `code`.
GET {{host}}/api/menu/{{basicModelCode}}?language=ar

### A specific country: selects the part prices and the labour rate on each line.
### An unmatched country is valid — parts fall back to price 0 and the line is flagged
### `hasUnpricedParts: true`, so the total is understated rather than silently wrong.
GET {{host}}/api/menu/{{basicModelCode}}?countryId=2

### Only the variants authored FREE OF CHARGE (All | FreeOnly | PaidOnly; All is the default).
### It selects VARIANTS — an excluded variant contributes neither its scheduled nor its standalone
### services — and it changes NO price: a free variant's lines carry the same totals any other variant's
### would, with `isFree: true` beside them. Render "free" from the flag; do not print the total.
###
### A filter that excludes every variant answers with no variants and `notFound: false`. The model HAS a
### menu; this request asked for a part of it that is empty.
GET {{host}}/api/menu/{{basicModelCode}}?freeFilter=FreeOnly

### ...and its complement: everything NOT flagged free.
GET {{host}}/api/menu/{{basicModelCode}}?freeFilter=PaidOnly

### ─────────────────── or reach the same menu from a VIN ───────────────────

### PREREQUISITE: these need the CompanyData/Vehicles containers, which this sample does NOT provision —
### menu replication only fills the Services database. Against a menus-only emulator they answer 503 and
### say so. Point ConnectionStrings:Cosmos at an account that also has vehicle data to run them.

### The vehicle lookup with the model's service menu attached.
###
### Everything above takes a basic model code as given. A vehicle lookup does not have one: it DERIVES it
### from the vehicle's Katashiki (first segment before the hyphen, trailing L/R dropped past five
### characters) and matches that against a code an author typed into the menus database. Nothing
### guarantees the two agree — that is open item O3 — so the response echoes all three:
###
###   katashiki       what the vehicle carries
###   basicModelCode  what was derived from it, and looked for — echoed even on a miss
###   serviceMenu.status  whether it matched, and if not, why
###
### status is the measurement: hit rate = Found / (Found + NotFound) over a real VIN population.
### NoBasicModelCode is NOT a miss — the vehicle had no Katashiki, so there was no key to join on.
### Unavailable / NotRegistered mean the menu subsystem could not be consulted; note the vehicle lookup
### still succeeded, because a menu fault is never allowed to fail it.
###
### An unknown VIN is an ordinary answer here, not a 404: no Katashiki, so NoBasicModelCode.
GET {{host}}/api/vehicle/{{vin}}

### Same vehicle, Arabic. Menu codes are language-dependent; correlate by `lineKey`, never by `code`.
GET {{host}}/api/vehicle/{{vin}}?language=ar

### A specific country for the part prices and labour rate on each line.
GET {{host}}/api/vehicle/{{vin}}?countryId=2

### An explicit transfer rate. It scales the consumable, so it moves the price quoted to a customer — and
### a caller-supplied value WINS over the host's CountrySettingsResolver, by design: a value that is
### silently ignored is worse than one that is absent. It moves no menu or labour CODE, because the
### labour-rate mapping is always keyed by the variant's primary rate.
###
### Bound from the query string here only because this sample is function-key protected. A public
### endpoint must fix it server-side, or leave it unset and let the resolver decide.
GET {{host}}/api/vehicle/{{vin}}?transferRate=1.15

### The free-of-charge filter, same three values as the menu endpoint. Every returned line carries
### `isFree` (the variant's flag, travelling on the line because the flat shape has no variant object),
### so a caller can equally ask for everything and group client-side.
###
### Excluding every variant leaves `status: "Found"` with no services — NOT `NotFound`, which is reserved
### for a model that has no menu at all and is counted as a join miss.
GET {{host}}/api/vehicle/{{vin}}?freeFilter=FreeOnly
